    "done_when": "in reckon/crew/recovery.py, _record_repair_dispatch and the within-round retry cap (REPAIR_RESUME_LIMIT) count a round's resume attempts keyed to that round's round_id: a round that has not been resumed starts at zero whatever earlier rounds of the same run recorded, and the report dispatch_repair_for_run returns carries the attempt it recorded. The run-wide cap of one automatic repair round per run (one-automatic-repair-round-per-run) is unchanged. tests/test_the_reflex_resumes_an_unpromoted_run.py gains a case where a run whose earlier round recorded two attempts opens a new round (with the run-wide cap stubbed open) and the new round's first resume records attempt 1, not 3. Only the named test files are run, with no call reaching SLURM and no real worker launched, each log ending with an EXIT= line; the coordinator runs the wider population at merge. Before status complete, delete every directory you created under /tmp, print what you delete, and list it in artifacts.",
